# Atlas — auth & tenancy (Sprint 02)
# Run against: dotnet run --project src/Atlas.Api

@host = http://localhost:5000

### Self-service signup: org + first admin + live session, atomically
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/register-org
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orgName": "Initech GmbH",
  "email": "ada@initech.example",
  "password": "correct-horse-battery",
  "displayName": "Ada Admin"
}

### Login (copy the token from the response)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ada@initech.example",
  "password": "correct-horse-battery"
}

### Who am I?
GET {{host}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

### Wrong password — SAME body as unknown user (no enumeration oracle)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ada@initech.example",
  "password": "wrong-password!"
}

### My own org → 200
GET {{host}}/api/v1/client-orgs/PASTE_YOUR_ORG_ID
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

### Someone else's org → 404 (NOT 403 — existence is need-to-know)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/client-orgs/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

### Platform staff: list every org (dev seed: ops@atlas.example / atlas-ops-dev-password)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ops@atlas.example",
  "password": "atlas-ops-dev-password"
}

### ...then:
GET {{host}}/api/v1/client-orgs?limit=10
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_OPS_TOKEN_HERE

### Logout (idempotent server-side; the token stops working)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_TOKEN_HERE
